            <div xml:id="d127">

                <pb facs="0284" n="199" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg199"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">422.11G93/1046: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hartman</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-12-27T11:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 27,
                                1919, 11 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>In the report of the Minister of Finance regarding the public debt which appeared
                    in <hi rendition="#italic">La Nation</hi> of November 23, the Minister charges
                    that the administration of the Railroad has not been upon an economic basis,
                    etc. Is the Department not correct then in its understanding <pb facs="0285"
                        n="200" xml:id="pg200"/> that no differences exist at present between the
                    Government and the Railroad?</p>
                <p>Department’s instruction No. 225 of October 24 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >4</hi>].</p>
                <p>You will request an answer from the Ecuadoran Government at its earliest
                    convenience.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
